llvm-4.0.0 backport patch: no nsw/nuw inferred on (A + C) from A's range, as 3.7 (PS4)

This patch CHANGES CODE GENERATION through ScalarEvolution's
StrengthenNoWrapFlags. r251048 (llvm-project 8f27415c05, 2015-10-22,
"[SCEV] Mark AddExprs as nsw or nuw if legal", first release LLVM 3.8)
asks for the signed and unsigned range of A when an add expression
(A + C) is built. That query computes the loop's backedge-taken count
before the zero extension of its induction variable is requested, the
unfolded extension stays in the unique table, and loop strength
reduction never sees the 64-bit recurrence 3.7 gives it (reduced
witness: `opt -analyze -iv-users` folds zext(i) under 3.7.1 and not
under 3.8.1, 3.9.1 or 4.0.0; round 233B). 0x583980, 0x583d80, 0x58b7c0
and 0xc060d0 are equal to the base in the prebuilt 3.7.1's module and
not under this line without the patch. With the patch those four compile
to the base's bytes, they are the only four of the module's 6,123
functions that change, and no matched game row changes (round 233B
built and swept this unconditional form alone; the supervisor repeated
the build and sweep with switchunh-01 and subscript-01).

diff -ru a/lib/Analysis/ScalarEvolution.cpp b/lib/Analysis/ScalarEvolution.cpp
--- a/lib/Analysis/ScalarEvolution.cpp
+++ b/lib/Analysis/ScalarEvolution.cpp
@@ -2047,7 +2047,6 @@
                       const SmallVectorImpl<const SCEV *> &Ops,
                       SCEV::NoWrapFlags Flags) {
   using namespace std::placeholders;
-  typedef OverflowingBinaryOperator OBO;
 
   bool CanAnalyze =
       Type == scAddExpr || Type == scAddRecExpr || Type == scMulExpr;
@@ -2067,29 +2066,9 @@
     Flags =
         ScalarEvolution::setFlags(Flags, (SCEV::NoWrapFlags)SignOrUnsignMask);
 
-  SignOrUnsignWrap = ScalarEvolution::maskFlags(Flags, SignOrUnsignMask);
-
-  if (SignOrUnsignWrap != SignOrUnsignMask && Type == scAddExpr &&
-      Ops.size() == 2 && isa<SCEVConstant>(Ops[0])) {
-
-    // (A + C) --> (A + C)<nsw> if the addition does not sign overflow
-    // (A + C) --> (A + C)<nuw> if the addition does not unsign overflow
-
-    const APInt &C = cast<SCEVConstant>(Ops[0])->getAPInt();
-    if (!(SignOrUnsignWrap & SCEV::FlagNSW)) {
-      auto NSWRegion = ConstantRange::makeGuaranteedNoWrapRegion(
-          Instruction::Add, C, OBO::NoSignedWrap);
-      if (NSWRegion.contains(SE->getSignedRange(Ops[1])))
-        Flags = ScalarEvolution::setFlags(Flags, SCEV::FlagNSW);
-    }
-    if (!(SignOrUnsignWrap & SCEV::FlagNUW)) {
-      auto NUWRegion = ConstantRange::makeGuaranteedNoWrapRegion(
-          Instruction::Add, C, OBO::NoUnsignedWrap);
-      if (NUWRegion.contains(SE->getUnsignedRange(Ops[1])))
-        Flags = ScalarEvolution::setFlags(Flags, SCEV::FlagNUW);
-    }
-  }
-
+  // PS4: no nsw/nuw inferred on (A + C) from A's range (r251048 not taken):
+  // the range query computed the loop's backedge-taken count before the
+  // extension of its induction variable was asked for.
   return Flags;
 }
 
